Iu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Cross-epic file-impact coordination (from RP-02 execution, 2026-08-18).\n\nRP-02 (epic 5e64-d9cd-2dd4-4036, citric-moudly-vipersquid) is decomposing binding_store.py into repository/lifecycle/recovery owners behind an unchanged facade, and is executing now. Three files in this task's impact set are being restructured underneath it:\n\n1. binding_store.py:110 `_env_int()` — reads os.environ for the binding lifecycle GC knobs (_DEFAULT_ABSENT_RETIRE_GRACE = 3 and the grace window). RP-02 S2 (fc1c-1b08-70c2-4afb, brainy-cooked-hog) MOVES this into the new src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_lifecycle.py. After S2 lands, this task's recorded target file for that read is stale — retarget to binding_lifecycle.py, symbol _env_int. RP-02 deliberately preserves the read's sourcing behavior byte-identically (still ambient, same defensive parse, same default/clamp) rather than pre-empting the seam cut, which is this task's slice. Note that the value feeds the three-miss + 3600-second keyless-unbind conjunction, whose behavior RP-02 S3 pins by acceptance criterion and drives through the environment in tests; a cut to an operation-snapshot source needs those tests updated in the same change.\n\n2. apply_handlers.py:210-214 `_rich_cutover_active()` — reads load_config().reconciler.rich_text_cutover. RP-02 S3 T3 rewrites the IMMEDIATELY ADJACENT _observe_rich_reemit (:223-273) to stop mutating through all_bindings(). Semantically independent, but adjacent hunks; RP-02 is keeping its diff tight to _observe_rich_reemit and not reflowing _rich_cutover_active.\n\n3. run_differs.py:685-688 max_acting_fraction — RP-02 S3 T2 inserts a pre-observation recovery call early in the pass (after preflight/lock, before remote fetch), so the edits are textually disjoint. Shared risk is the module cap: the file is 739/800, so both slices are drawing on 61 lines of headroom.\n\nRecorded as relates_to, NOT depends_on: per docs/ticket-model.md:184-190 a blocking relation between a task here and a story under RP-02 would escalate to a full RP-04-epic <-> RP-02-epic blocker. Same reasoning RP-02 S3 already documented for its RP-04 S3 coupling. Overlapping file impact stays visible without freezing either root.\n\nNo pause requested. RP-02 lands first by design — this task cannot correctly cut a read whose home is about to move, and RP-02 relieves the 799/800 pressure on binding_store.py that currently blocks anyone from adding a line to it.","timestamp":1787096348230815001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"C3a complete — both child slices landed and closed: C3a-CORE (ba8b, Gerrit 1898 merged d361eb28e4) + C3a-JIRA (a34b, landed earlier). All 35 C3a files drained from LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS; check_config_ownership.py exit 0. Only residual reconciler rows are the 2 binding_lifecycle.py entries owned by S7.3.a (moved there by an origin/main refactor), not C3a. Subsystem suites green (Verified+1 on both changes).","timestamp":1787137853348009001}],"created_at":1787095104408880001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ee7d2e9e-85f8-48d8-9875-b2111747718d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fc1c-1b08-70c2-4afb"},{"link_uuid":"4fa6a735-8913-4fcf-9a27-e0e283bd4baa","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"01d8-c18d-b229-419a"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nSlice C1 (ticket 29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8) recorded 57 below-seam ambient config/credential reads in the reconciler engine (_engine/rebar_reconciler + _engine_support) as entries in `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS`. RP-04 is not complete while these ambient reads sit below the approved composition/credential/backend seams enforced by `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`. Parent: 075b-1479-dcb7-40ab.\n\nAffected files (relative to `src/rebar/`):\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_advisory_lock.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_preflight.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/access_check.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/settings.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_handlers.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_planning.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_walk.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_differ.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_translate.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/invariants.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/last_pass.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_comments.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/pass_io.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/rebar_id_audit.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_check.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/request.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/run_differs.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck_visibility.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine_support/lookups.py`\n  - `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py`\n\n## Outcome\nEvery below-seam read in the files above is either (a) CUT to compose through the approved seam that already assembles config — the operation snapshot (`rebar._operation_config.OperationSnapshot` / `compose_operation_snapshot`), a startup binding, or the provider-credential boundary — or (b) REGISTERED as an owned, non-legacy entry with an exact `path`+`symbol`+`rationale` for genuine test-only controls and protocol constants. Their `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` entries are removed. `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` reports zero findings for these paths with those entries gone and no path-glob exception. The subsystem's behavioral suites stay green; redacted operation-snapshot fingerprints / provider-neutral outcomes are unchanged except recorded, justified deltas.\n\n## Plan\n1. For each below-seam read in the listed files, classify as cut-to-seam or register-owned; for cut-to-seam, thread the value from the composition seam rather than reading ambient `os.environ`/`os.getenv`/`load_config` below it.\n2. Remove the corresponding entries for these files from `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` in `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`.\n3. Run `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and the subsystem behavioral suites (tests/interfaces/store, tests/integration reconciler suites, tests/unit/rebar_reconciler); keep green.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- Held-out test `tests/scripts/test_reconciler_engine_seam_clean_heldout.py` asserts `check_config_ownership.check(check_config_ownership.REPO_ROOT)` returns no finding string containing any of the listed paths, AND that `config_ownership_exceptions.LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` contains zero entries whose `path` is one of the listed files. RED now (entries present + reads below seam).\n- The subsystem behavioral suites (tests/interfaces/store, tests/integration reconciler suites, tests/unit/rebar_reconciler) stay green after the cutover — they are the correctness oracle the AST gate supplements.\n- Redacted operation-snapshot fingerprints before/after are equal except recorded deltas.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nNo stored ticket/event/binding format changes. A legacy facade is removed only after its focused suite passes; until then rollback selects the facade.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] No direct ambient config/credential read, backend reload, or configurable default remains below the approved seam in the 35 listed files; each is cut-to-seam or registered as an owned (non-legacy) entry with rationale.\n- [x] The `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` entries for these files are removed from `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`, and `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` passes with no path-glob exception (proven by the held-out `test_reconciler_engine_seam_clean_heldout.py`).\n- [x] The subsystem behavioral suites (tests/interfaces/store, tests/integration reconciler suites, tests/unit/rebar_reconciler) pass after the cutover; redacted operation-snapshot fingerprints / provider-neutral outcomes are unchanged except recorded approved deltas.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py","reason":"Cut below-seam config/credential read to the approved seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_advisory_lock.py","reason":"Cut below-seam config/credential read to the approved seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_preflight.py","reason":"Cut below-seam config/credential read to the approved seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/access_check.py","reason":"Cut below-seam config/credential read to the approved seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py","reason":"Cut below-seam config/credential read to the approved seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_en